{"uid":"modules/hash_cracker.py","name":"hash_cracker.py","qualname":"modules/hash_cracker.py","kind":"module","file":"modules/hash_cracker.py","line":1,"end_line":726,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Hash cracking pipeline — John the Ripper and Hashcat integration.","description":"Parses hash formats from secretsdump output, identifies hash types, and\nruns the appropriate cracker. Results feed back into the LazyOwnDB\ncredentials table.\n\nDesign (SOLID):\n- Single Responsibility: HashCracker only cracks hashes.\n- Open/Closed: new hash formats added via HASH_FORMATS dict.\n- Liskov: any cracker (John, Hashcat) implements CrackBackend protocol.\n- Interface Segregation: identify(), crack(), and import_results().\n- Dependency Inversion: depends on abstract backend, not concrete binary.\n\nUsage:\n    from modules.hash_cracker import HashCracker\n\n    cracker = HashCracker(wordlist=\"/usr/share/wordlists/rockyou.txt\")\n    results = cracker.crack_file(\"sessions/hashes_10.10.11.5.txt\")\n    cracker.import_to_db(results, rhost=\"10.10.11.5\")","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["modules/hash_cracker.py::HASH_PATTERNS","modules/hash_cracker.py::COMMON_WORDLISTS","modules/hash_cracker.py::CrackResult","modules/hash_cracker.py::HashIdentifier","modules/hash_cracker.py::HashCracker","modules/hash_cracker.py::crack_secretsdump_output"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
